{
  "determination": true,
  "inputs": [
    {
      "rust_file": "src/output.rs",
      "rust_item": "impl[Output]/fn[normal]",
      "text": [
        "    // {impl}`design.requirements.output.messages_stdout`",
        "    // {impl}`design.requirements.output.warnings_stderr`",
        "    pub fn normal() -> Self {",
        "        Self {",
        "            quiet: false,",
        "            capture: None,",
        "        }",
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rust_file": "src/output.rs",
      "rust_item": "impl[Output]/fn[emit_err]",
      "text": [
        "    // {impl}`design.requirements.output.quiet`",
        "    // {impl}`design.requirements.output.capture`",
        "    // {impl}`design.requirements.output.warnings_stderr`",
        "    fn emit_err(&self, msg: String) {",
        "        if self.quiet {",
        "            return;",
        "        }",
        "        if let Some(buf) = &self.capture {",
        "            buf.lock().unwrap().push(msg);",
        "        } else {",
        "            eprintln!(\"{msg}\");",
        "        }",
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rust_file": "src/output.rs",
      "rust_item": "impl[Output]/fn[warn]",
      "text": [
        "    /// A warning (something went wrong but not fatal).",
        "    // {impl}`design.requirements.output.quiet`",
        "    // {impl}`design.requirements.output.capture`",
        "    // {impl}`design.requirements.output.warnings_stderr`",
        "    pub fn warn(&self, msg: impl std::fmt::Display) {",
        "        self.emit_err(format!(\"⚠️  {msg}\"));",
        "    }"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "`Output::normal()` sets `quiet: false, capture: None`. `warn` formats `⚠️  {msg}` and calls `emit_err`, which, not quiet and not capturing, calls `eprintln!` (stderr). `warn` is the only helper routed to `emit_err`.\n\nUntested: no test runs a normal `Output` and inspects stderr. Judged from code, which is a direct three-branch function.",
  "requirement": "A normal `Output` MUST print warnings to stderr."
}
